# Experiment 10, in one file: the same plant as 03-compact, built upwards.
#
# 03-compact answers the power brief on 72 tiles of plot by packing everything
# onto the slab. This answers it -- same power, same fuel, same water -- on 60,
# by putting the second exchanger train on a mezzanine over the first. That is
# the whole of what experiment 10 added to the document: `up`, and `face`.
#
# What it costs is visible from the outside. The deck needs columns down to
# the ground, an edge, a handrail and a flight of stairs, all of which appear
# without being asked for and all of which take up room the spatial rules then
# measure. What it buys is a third of the footprint -- and the brief asks for
# footprint, so this is a real trade rather than a decoration.
#
# The `face` lines are doing work too. Each train is turned so that it points
# along the row, rather than wherever the flow inference would have pointed it,
# and the drive trains come out straight enough that `machine space` has
# nothing to say about them -- which is more than can be said for most of the
# designs in this directory.
#
# It is not perfect, and it is more interesting for not being. Two yellows:
#
#   the pump is a metre from a reactor, which is hot
#   the upper exchanger is boxed in on all four sides
#
# Both are the cost of the packing, both would be fixed by giving something a
# tile of room, and both are exactly the trade the spatial rules exist to make
# visible. `machine space designs/17-stacked.machine` says so.

machine "Stacked"
brief power

reactor   R1  at 0,0  throttle 40

# The ground floor: reactor, one exchanger train, and the feedwater pump.
exchanger HX1 at 4,0        face east
turbine   T1  at 7,0        face east
generator G1  at 10,0       face east

pump      W1  at 4,3

# And the second train, six metres up, directly over the first.
exchanger HX2 at 4,0,3      face east
turbine   T2  at 7,0,3      face east
generator G2  at 10,0,3     face east

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W1.water -> HX2.water

wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T2.steam

wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
wire T2.rotary -> G2.rotary
